#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078245 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "982052d0-32dc-557a-b501-cfb011787f22" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating a Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using a Tangent Line Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "63a9a3bd-b7ce-5c1d-a138-0bc8f8f87ce6" :question/math-academy-id "e-536" :question/problem "For the initial value problem\n\n$y' = 2xy, \\qquad y(1)=2$,\n\nuse the tangent line approximation at $x=1$ to approximate $y\\left(\\dfrac 3 2\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation to $y(x)$ at the point $a=1$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(x) &= y(a) + y^{′}(a)(x - a) \\\\\n&= y(1) + y^{′}(1)(x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the initial condition, we know that $y(1) = 2$. We also know that\n\n$$\ny'(x) = 2xy\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny'(1) = 2(1)(2) = 4\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $y(1)$ and $y'(1)$ into our expression for $L(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(x) &= 2 + (4)(x - 1) \\\\\n&= 2 + 4x - 4 \\\\\n&= 4x - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can approximate\n\n$$\ny\\left(\\dfrac 3 2\\right)\n$$\n\nusing\n\n$$\nL\\left(\\dfrac 3 2\\right)\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\ny\\left(\\dfrac 3 2 \\right)\\approx L\\left(\\dfrac 3 2 \\right) = 4\\left(\\dfrac 3 2\\right) - 2 = 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078287 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e731217-ca61-5295-aeb5-0c3febd250d8" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the First Row of a Table Using Euler's Method"}] :question/id #uuid "45166435-4bf0-5356-baa3-436258817620" :question/math-academy-id "e-7700" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$y' =7x-2y, \\qquad y(1)=-4$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the column for $\\Delta y$ in the table below if the step size is $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{1}{10}$?\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ |  |  | $\\,? \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(1)=-4$, we fill $y=-4$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $-4$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $y'$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= 7x - 2y \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot 1 - 2 \\cdot (-4) \\\\\n&= 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $-4$ | $15$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $\\Delta y$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔy &= y^{′} \\cdot Δx \\\\\n&= 15 \\cdot \\frac{1}{10} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $-4$ | $15$ | $\\dfrac{3}{2}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078298 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0eb0c7f2-a559-5324-8778-ca5cab083864" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating the Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using Euler's Method With One Step"}] :question/id #uuid "53e498a9-cb99-57bf-9b24-3cf67dc9a021" :question/math-academy-id "e-9340" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$y' =2y^2-x^2, \\qquad y(1)=3$\n\nUse Euler's method with one step to approximate $y(2)$." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2$, we will use a step size of\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = 2-1 = 1\n$$\n\nFirst, we add the initial condition data:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $3$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $y'$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= 2y^{2} - x^{2} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3^{2} - 1^{2} \\\\\n&= 18 - 1 \\\\\n&= 17\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $17$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $\\Delta y$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔy &= y^{′} \\cdot Δx \\\\\n&= 17 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 17\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $17$ | $17$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $\\Delta x$ to $x$ and $\\Delta y$ to $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{new} &= x + Δx \\\\\n&= 1 + 1 \\\\\n&= 2 \\\\\ny_{new} &= y + Δy \\\\\n&= 3 + 17 \\\\\n&= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\, y'\\,$ | $\\, \\Delta y \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $17$ | $17$ |\n| $2$ | $20$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(2) \\approx 20\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "982052d0-32dc-557a-b501-cfb011787f22" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating a Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using a Tangent Line Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86bee354-eded-5d9a-b0a7-f32c77cd34b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076996} {:answer/id #uuid "c03b31fa-49e1-56d7-bbf5-fc10f5f27918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076997} {:answer/id #uuid "460765da-0359-51f6-a5b8-1fb2ddd098a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076998} {:answer/id #uuid "4dddb5e9-6375-5eae-966e-ad326375a496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076999} {:answer/id #uuid "60fd45dd-105d-52b6-89d8-b24be6f4cd61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86bee354-eded-5d9a-b0a7-f32c77cd34b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076996} :answer-field/id #uuid "a86dbc34-dbf5-5b63-9e60-9d494ebe026b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076995}] :question/id #uuid "9f352ca6-2003-56c9-a6e6-ea5f1e44d59d" :question/math-academy-id "q-50119" :question/problem "Consider the initial value problem\n\n$y^{′} = y(x - 4), y(0) = 1$.\n\nUse the tangent line approximation of $y(x)$ at $x = 0$ to approximate $y(1)$."}]}
